# docs/_internal/ — agent-facing working documents

This tree is the project's reasoning record: decision traces, dated handoffs, research
notes, and the stable scientific framing. It is agent-facing, not the published
deliverable. Public-facing material lives under `docs/` outside `_internal/`.

## Layout

| Path | Holds |
|------|-------|
| `scientific-context.md` | stable scientific framing (question, datasets, goals) |
| `reasoning/` | decision traces, why-not logs, agent thinking |
| `sessions/` | dated session handoffs |
| `ai-generated/research/` | literature / web research notes |

## Naming conventions

| Pattern | Used for |
|---------|----------|
| `YYYY-MM-DD_NN_topic.md` | research notes and explorations (`NN` = within-day sequence) |
| `YYYY-MM-DD_<slug>.md` | session handoffs |
| `<slug>.md` | decisions and ADRs (dateless) |

`NN` is the within-day sequence number. Compute it from the files already present for
today's date:

```bash
printf "%02d" $(( $(ls dir/ | grep "^$DATE" | wc -l) + 1 ))
```

## One-way reference rule

`docs/_internal/` may reference any public artifact (scripts, results, config keys).
The reverse is forbidden: public-facing files must NOT link to or mention `_internal/`.
